// __nUlakam/vaZporuL/vaZporuL.qmz — வன்பொருள் (hardware): pins, time, serial__
// வன்பொருள்: முனைகள், நேரம், தொடர்த் துறை
//
// __One hardware vocabulary for every board eTamil runs on, so the same program__
// __drives a Raspberry Pi and an Arduino:__
//
//   __etamil --vm prog.qmz                   Raspberry Pi: real GPIO and serial ports__
//   __ETAMIL_BOARD=sim etamil --vm prog.qmz  any machine: a simulated board, for tests__
//   __etamil --artino --board uno prog.qmz   Arduino: compiled (docs/artino.md)__
//
// __Beside this file, one per board, are its pin names: yUnO.qmz (Uno), nAnO.qmz__
// __(Nano), mekA.qmz (Mega), pIkO.qmz (Pico and Pico 2), rAspY.qmz (Raspberry Pi).__
// __Each imports this file, so a program imports its board's file and nothing__
// __else, and names விளக்கு_முனை or ஒப்புமை_0 rather than 13 or 14.__
//
// __On the VM each function is a thin layer over a host builtin, called by its__
// ___english alias. Board state — pin levels, simulated time, serial buffers —__
// __lives in the host, because an eTamil function cannot change a module's__
// __variables. Under artino the compiler maps these same names to the board's__
// __own calls and does not run this file's bodies.__
//
// __Two rules shape the surface:__
// __- Pin and time calls return plain values. A pin that cannot be driven is a__
// __  wiring or permission mistake, found the first time the program runs, so it__
// __  stops the program with the host's message rather than becoming a result__
// __  every caller must check.__
// __- A serial port can be absent or unplugged at any time, so opening one gives__
// __  a result (சரி or தவறு) that the program is expected to handle.__
//
// __The VM's side is src/vm/board.rs: the simulated board anywhere, a Raspberry__
// __Pi's pins through the Linux GPIO device, and serial ports by device path on__
// __Linux and macOS.__

// __--- the board --------------------------------------------------------------__

// __Split into the files below. This one keeps the name so that every__
// __`இறக்கு` of it still reaches every function it used to.__

இறக்கு "muZY.qmz";
இறக்கு "nEram.qmz";
இறக்கு "qotarqquRY.qmz";
இறக்கு "pOli.qmz";
